package gate

// K7G12Corpus is the G12 corpus of ADR-0037 (the owner's decision on
// ADR-0035), generated by internal/synth (gencorpus --set k7): G12 judged
// outside fault windows for plans of contract 1.2.0 or later, and the same
// fault-overlapped storms under the literal rule.
const K7G12Corpus = "testdata/corpus-k7"

// K7G12SabotageDeps is, for each checker sabotage rule G12 depends on
// (build tag cp_sabotage_<rule>), the set of corpus-k7 labels whose
// histories must stop matching their expected.json when that rule is
// broken — and no others. Written from ADR-0037 and the plants of
// internal/synth/k7.go, before any sabotage build ran:
//
//   - fair_share: no starvation anomaly is reported: the
//     fair-share-starvation plants and the g12-literal plants (the literal
//     rule's starvation).
//   - g12_fault_exclusion: operations invoked inside fault windows are
//     judged: the overload-fault-overlap plants fail (their literal
//     fraction is below 90 %), and the not-judged plants are judged and
//     fail (every operation inside their fault failed). The starvation
//     plants still fail and keep their observations; clean plants have no
//     operation inside a fault window during a storm.
//   - g12_judged_minimum: no minimum rate: the not-judged plants pass (the
//     sparse ones' two judged operations are ok; the empty ones have none).
var K7G12SabotageDeps = map[string][]string{
	"fair_share":          {"fair-share-starvation", "g12-literal"},
	"g12_fault_exclusion": {"overload-fault-overlap", "fair-share-not-judged"},
	"g12_judged_minimum":  {"fair-share-not-judged"},
}
